# atlas — Docker build context trimmer (shared by Dockerfile + Dockerfile.web).
#
# Build context is `projects/atlas/` (NOT the repo root) for BOTH images. Each
# image runs its own isolated `pnpm install` inside the build, so committed
# node_modules / build outputs / local env / test surfaces are dead weight (and
# a security risk for .env). The build context MUST still include the
# `atlas-shared` package at the project root (`src/` + the root package.json) —
# both images need it (the server imports its Zod-runtime + geo impl, the web
# imports its WS-frame types + client geo impl), so `src/` is deliberately NOT
# excluded here. The apex lesson (inline what the build context must resolve) is
# honoured by COPYing the root manifest + `tsconfig.base.json` + `src/` in the
# Dockerfiles; nothing below excludes them.
#
# Keep ONLY what the stages COPY: the umbrella manifest (package.json =
# atlas-shared) + tsconfig.base.json, src/ (atlas-shared source), server/{src,
# scripts,drizzle,*.json,*.config.*}, web/{src,public,*.json,*.config.*}, the
# entrypoint, and the Dockerfiles themselves.

# --- dependencies (each stage installs its own) ---
**/node_modules

# --- build outputs (rebuilt inside the image) ---
**/.next
**/.turbo
**/coverage
**/dist
**/out
**/.cache
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/.eslintcache
**/playwright/.cache

# --- env + secrets (NEVER ship .env into an image) ---
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# --- local data / docker compose (local-only) ---
docker-compose.yml
**/*.sqlite
**/*.sqlite3

# --- the keyless basemap extract is a LARGE BINARY, gitignored + generated at
#     deploy time and dropped into web/public/map/porto.pmtiles. It is NOT in
#     the repo; exclude it defensively so a locally-generated copy is not
#     uploaded in the context (the web image serves it from the same path once
#     placed there at deploy — see DEPLOY.md). The committed keyless graticule
#     fallback renders WITHOUT it.
web/public/map/*.pmtiles

# --- tests, smoke scripts, review artifacts, coverage (not needed at runtime) ---
e2e
**/__tests__
**/__fixtures__
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test.tsx
**/*.spec.ts
**/*.spec.tsx
**/playwright.config.ts
**/playwright-report
**/test-results
**/.lighthouseci
lighthouserc.json
web/lighthouserc.json
# NOTE: server/scripts/seed.ts is NEEDED at runtime (the entrypoint runs it on
# boot), so server/scripts is NOT excluded. server/scripts/ws-smoke.ts is a dev
# smoke and harmless to ship; it is never invoked by the entrypoint.

# --- docs + meta (the runtime never reads these) ---
PLAN.md
DECISIONS.md
PROGRESS.md
AGENT_NOTES.md
CHANGELOG.md
README.md
DEPLOY.md
**/*.md
.github
docs

# --- the build / deploy descriptors themselves ---
fly.toml
fly.web.toml
Dockerfile
Dockerfile.web
.dockerignore

# --- editor / OS noise ---
.vscode
.idea
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db

# --- logs ---
**/*.log
**/npm-debug.log*

# --- git metadata ---
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
